---
description: Release and production safety rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Cursor does not create or approve Production Release decisions.
- Never edit releases/, deploy/, ci/, GitHub workflows, or release policy merely to make a failing release pass.
- A Release must bind to a locked Build Spec, closed Sprint(s), source commit, passing gate results, and User approval.
- Release manifests may select only supported deployment target types; never add arbitrary shell commands.
- Production database migrations are forward-only and must be backward-compatible / expand-only.
- Never auto-generate a destructive DB rollback.
- Production code rollback is allowed only through the governed rollback workflow.
- A release failure is a Finding / Incident input; it does not change product truth.
